        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Pin managed Linux bootstrap installers",
        "body": "Closes #715.\n\nManaged Linux bootstrap no longer emits root `curl | sh` installer pipelines for Code or Tailscale. Code-server installs from pinned release tarballs with SHA-256 verification, and Tailscale always uses the checksum-verified static archive path.\n\nCompatibility note: legacy `CRABBOX_TAILSCALE_INSTALL_MODE=package` now maps to the pinned static archive path; preserving package-mode semantics would require a separate signed repository path.\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent landing candidate: `7d3028c4166a4c8a7b26b62b39a9e9e6987bfea2`, rebased onto current `main`.\n\n- verified both code-server 4.126.0 asset digests against the official GitHub release metadata\n- verified both Tailscale 1.98.4 archive digests against the official `.sha256` endpoints\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli`\n- 24 Worker test files, 697 tests\n- focused final-base Code/Tailscale tests and Worker typecheck\n- autoreview clean\n\n## Remaining Live Gate\n\nExact-head proof should boot a managed Linux canary with both Code and Tailscale enabled, confirm the pinned binaries start, and confirm the node joins the tailnet with a `100.x` address. The maintainer environment has a running Tailscale client but no reusable auth key or OAuth client credential.\n\nRequired decision/input: one one-off ephemeral Tailscale auth key authorized to own `tag:crabbox`. The key must not be posted to the PR; inject it only for the validation run.\n",
        "branch": "harden-crabbox-linux-bootstrap-715",
